    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d185-a1">

                <pb facs="0306" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg226"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wilcox to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-03-05"><hi rendition="#italic">March 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to forward applications for
                    passports for Messrs. Ruhl and Snyder to return to their mission in eastern
                    Thibet. I received their passports Nos. 367 and 365, but while they give them
                    permission to travel in Hupeh, Szechuen, and Kansuh, they do not permit them to
                    travel in Thibet.</p>
                <pb facs="0307" n="227" xml:id="pg227"/>
                <p>They desire to leave here by April 5. I would therefore inquire if a special
                    permit can not be granted to them (separately) to return to their mission in
                    Thibet?</p>
                <p>Awaiting your early reply, I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. S. Wilcox</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
